title Ghost pedalling: driving at 160 W on effort level 3, then spinning the cranks without pushing (physics)

# On a torque-sensor bike, legs turning without pushing get no assist. With
# a cadence sensor, legs spinning slower than the chainring (the freewheel
# turning) look like pedalling. The wheel sensor gives the gear (PAS edges
# per wheel turn) while the cranks drive; drifting off it means the legs
# are freewheeling, and effort assist gives nothing.
bike pedal_stroke 0.8
bike pas_edge_error_deg 0.3
config level 3 effort_x10 15
config level 3 target_current_percent 60

at 0 level 0
at 0 speed 32
at 0 gear 3.0
at 0 grade -2
at 0 rider_w 150
at 190000 rider_w 0
at 190000 brake 1
at 199000 brake 0

at 200000 grade 2
at 200000 gear 1.6
at 200000 level 3
at 200000 rider_w 160
# stop pushing, keep turning the cranks at 45 rpm, slower than the chainring
at 220000 rider_w 0
at 220000 spin 45
# push again
at 230000 spin 0
at 230000 rider_w 160

end 245000

# driving: effort assist (1.5x the estimate)
expect 219000 current >= 10
# spinning slower than the bike: nothing, from ~1.5 s in
expect 222500 current == 0
expect 229500 current == 0
# pushing again: assist back within ~3 s
expect 233000 current >= 10
